{"module":"policing","voice":"male","duration":260.3,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"La policía y la llamada al 911","start":0.0,"end":3.52,"words":[[0.02,0.21],[0.21,0.98],[0.98,1.07],[1.07,1.26],[1.26,1.84],[1.84,2.03],[2.03,3.46]]},{"el":"intro","text":"La Ley CAREN trata de un daño específico: llamar a la policía contra alguien por su raza.","start":4.32,"end":10.4,"words":[[4.34,4.49],[4.49,4.71],[4.71,5.08],[5.08,5.45],[5.45,5.6],[5.6,5.75],[5.75,6.05],[6.05,6.86],[7.12,7.49],[7.49,7.57],[7.57,7.72],[7.72,8.31],[8.31,8.76],[8.76,9.2],[9.2,9.42],[9.42,9.57],[9.57,9.94]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Este módulo muestra de dónde viene ese daño y por qué una llamada puede ser peligrosa.","start":10.75,"end":15.84,"words":[[10.75,11.02],[11.02,11.43],[11.43,11.91],[11.91,12.04],[12.04,12.38],[12.38,12.72],[12.72,12.93],[12.93,13.2],[13.2,13.27],[13.27,13.47],[13.47,13.61],[13.61,13.81],[13.81,14.22],[14.22,14.56],[14.56,14.76],[14.76,15.44]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Patrullas de esclavos","start":16.19,"end":17.74,"words":[[16.22,16.9],[16.9,17.05],[17.05,17.65]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Desde la ley de Carolina del Sur de 1704, las colonias y estados del Sur organizaron patrullas de esclavos: hombres blancos que recorrían de noche, detenían a personas negras, exigían pases, registraban las viviendas de los esclavizados y azotaban a quienes encontraban sin permiso.","start":18.44,"end":39.42,"words":[[18.47,18.85],[18.85,19.0],[19.0,19.23],[19.23,19.38],[19.38,19.98],[19.98,20.21],[20.21,20.43],[20.43,20.58],[20.58,22.16],[22.43,22.65],[22.65,23.26],[23.26,23.33],[23.33,23.86],[23.86,24.09],[24.09,24.31],[24.31,25.14],[25.14,25.82],[25.82,25.97],[25.97,26.65],[26.91,27.36],[27.36,27.89],[27.89,28.04],[28.04,28.72],[28.72,28.87],[28.87,29.32],[29.59,30.27],[30.27,30.34],[30.34,30.94],[30.94,31.47],[31.74,32.41],[32.41,32.87],[33.13,33.96],[33.96,34.18],[34.18,34.86],[34.86,35.01],[35.01,35.24],[35.24,36.14],[36.14,36.22],[36.22,36.82],[36.82,36.9],[36.9,37.35],[37.35,38.18],[38.18,38.41],[38.41,39.01]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Se esperaba que toda persona blanca ayudara a vigilar a los esclavizados.","start":39.77,"end":45.1,"words":[[39.78,39.94],[39.94,40.59],[40.59,40.75],[40.75,41.07],[41.07,41.63],[41.63,42.12],[42.12,42.68],[42.68,42.76],[42.76,43.33],[43.33,43.41],[43.41,43.65],[43.65,44.7]]},{"el":"h1","text":"De las patrullas a la policía","start":46.0,"end":48.24,"words":[[46.06,46.23],[46.23,46.48],[46.48,47.22],[47.22,47.31],[47.31,47.47],[47.47,48.14]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Tras la emancipación, muchas funciones de las patrullas del Sur pasaron a la nueva policía municipal y a los alguaciles.","start":48.94,"end":57.31,"words":[[48.96,49.26],[49.26,49.41],[49.41,50.4],[50.66,51.12],[51.12,51.8],[51.8,51.95],[51.95,52.17],[52.17,52.85],[52.85,53.08],[53.08,53.31],[53.31,53.84],[53.84,53.91],[53.91,54.06],[54.06,54.44],[54.44,55.05],[55.05,55.73],[55.73,55.8],[55.8,55.88],[55.88,56.1],[56.1,56.93]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Qué tan directa es la línea entre las patrullas y la policía moderna se debate: los departamentos del Norte (Boston 1838, Nueva York 1845) surgieron sobre todo del modelo de Londres y del control de inmigrantes y trabajadores.","start":57.66,"end":74.76,"words":[[57.69,57.83],[57.83,58.03],[58.03,58.51],[58.51,58.64],[58.64,58.78],[58.78,59.12],[59.12,59.46],[59.46,59.66],[59.66,60.28],[60.28,60.34],[60.34,60.48],[60.48,61.02],[61.02,61.5],[61.5,61.63],[61.63,62.11],[62.35,62.55],[62.55,63.44],[63.44,63.64],[63.64,63.98],[63.98,64.39],[64.39,66.29],[66.53,66.87],[66.87,67.14],[67.14,69.04],[69.28,69.89],[69.89,70.23],[70.23,70.51],[70.51,70.71],[70.71,71.12],[71.12,71.25],[71.25,71.73],[71.73,71.8],[71.8,72.0],[72.0,72.48],[72.48,72.61],[72.61,73.36],[73.36,73.43],[73.43,74.31]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Los historiadores coinciden en que en el Sur la tarea de controlar el movimiento de las personas negras continuó.","start":75.11,"end":82.04,"words":[[75.15,75.36],[75.36,76.21],[76.21,76.84],[76.84,76.98],[76.98,77.12],[77.12,77.26],[77.26,77.4],[77.4,77.62],[77.62,77.76],[77.76,78.11],[78.11,78.25],[78.25,78.88],[78.88,79.02],[79.02,79.73],[79.73,79.87],[79.87,80.08],[80.08,80.64],[80.64,81.06],[81.06,81.7]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Códigos Negros, leyes de vagancia y arrendamiento de presos","start":82.94,"end":87.26,"words":[[82.96,83.47],[83.47,83.98],[84.24,84.6],[84.6,84.75],[84.75,85.33],[85.33,85.4],[85.4,86.27],[86.27,86.42],[86.42,86.86]]},{"el":"s2","text":"La Decimotercera Enmienda (1865) abolió la esclavitud “excepto como castigo por un delito”.","start":87.96,"end":95.45,"words":[[87.99,88.13],[88.13,89.04],[89.04,89.61],[89.61,91.5],[91.74,92.16],[92.16,92.3],[92.3,93.0],[93.0,93.49],[93.49,93.77],[93.77,94.27],[94.27,94.48],[94.48,94.62],[94.62,95.11]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Los estados del Sur aprobaron de inmediato Códigos Negros que convertían en delito que las personas negras estuvieran desempleadas, caminaran de noche o “merodearan”.","start":95.8,"end":105.78,"words":[[95.84,96.04],[96.04,96.51],[96.51,96.71],[96.71,96.91],[96.91,97.5],[97.5,97.64],[97.64,98.24],[98.24,98.7],[98.7,99.1],[99.1,99.23],[99.23,99.97],[99.97,100.1],[100.1,100.5],[100.5,100.63],[100.63,100.83],[100.83,101.36],[101.36,101.76],[101.76,102.43],[102.43,103.29],[103.52,104.12],[104.12,104.26],[104.26,104.59],[104.59,104.66],[104.66,105.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Los arrestados eran arrendados a plantaciones, minas y ferrocarriles, y a menudo morían a tasas más altas que bajo la esclavitud.","start":106.13,"end":115.29,"words":[[106.15,106.39],[106.39,107.09],[107.09,107.4],[107.4,108.1],[108.1,108.17],[108.17,109.18],[109.45,109.84],[109.84,109.92],[109.92,110.85],[111.12,111.2],[111.2,111.28],[111.28,111.74],[111.74,112.29],[112.29,112.36],[112.36,112.75],[112.75,112.98],[112.98,113.37],[113.37,113.53],[113.53,113.84],[113.84,113.99],[113.99,114.85]]},{"el":"s2","text":"El arrendamiento de presos duró en Alabama hasta 1928.","start":115.64,"end":120.76,"words":[[115.66,115.8],[115.8,116.68],[116.68,116.82],[116.82,117.26],[117.26,117.55],[117.55,117.7],[117.7,118.21],[118.21,118.5],[118.5,120.4]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Una acusación podía ser una sentencia de muerte","start":121.66,"end":124.92,"words":[[121.72,121.95],[121.95,122.65],[122.65,123.12],[123.12,123.36],[123.36,123.59],[123.59,124.29],[124.29,124.45],[124.45,124.92]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Muchos linchamientos empezaron con una acusación de una persona blanca.","start":125.62,"end":131.02,"words":[[125.64,126.11],[126.11,127.13],[127.13,127.84],[127.84,128.08],[128.08,128.32],[128.32,129.03],[129.03,129.18],[129.18,129.42],[129.42,129.97],[129.97,130.52]]},{"el":"s3","text":"En 1955, el relato de Carolyn Bryant sobre un encuentro en una tienda de Misisipi llevó al asesinato de Emmett Till, de 14 años.","start":131.37,"end":142.07,"words":[[131.39,131.53],[131.53,133.71],[133.97,134.11],[134.11,134.55],[134.55,134.69],[134.69,135.2],[135.2,135.71],[135.71,136.07],[136.07,136.22],[136.22,136.87],[136.87,137.02],[137.02,137.23],[137.23,137.67],[137.67,137.82],[137.82,138.4],[138.4,138.69],[138.69,138.83],[138.83,139.49],[139.49,139.63],[139.63,140.07],[140.07,140.36],[140.61,140.76],[140.76,141.27],[141.27,141.63]]},{"el":"s3","text":"(En un libro de 2017, el historiador Timothy Tyson informó que ella admitió después que partes de su relato no eran ciertas; su familia lo niega.","start":142.42,"end":152.8,"words":[[142.45,142.6],[142.6,142.75],[142.75,143.12],[143.12,143.27],[143.27,144.52],[144.78,144.93],[144.93,145.67],[145.67,146.12],[146.12,146.49],[146.49,147.01],[147.01,147.15],[147.15,147.45],[147.45,147.97],[147.97,148.49],[148.49,148.64],[148.64,149.08],[149.08,149.23],[149.23,149.38],[149.38,149.82],[149.82,149.97],[149.97,150.27],[150.27,150.86],[151.12,151.27],[151.27,151.78],[151.78,151.93],[151.93,152.38]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Ese detalle está debatido.)","start":153.15,"end":155.52,"words":[[153.17,153.43],[153.43,154.02],[154.02,154.36],[154.36,155.13]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La lección en la que se basa la Ley CAREN es más antigua que cualquier caso: cuando la persona denunciada es negra, la respuesta policial puede ser mortal.","start":155.87,"end":165.21,"words":[[155.89,156.02],[156.02,156.49],[156.49,156.63],[156.63,156.76],[156.76,156.9],[156.9,157.03],[157.03,157.3],[157.3,157.44],[157.44,157.64],[157.64,157.98],[157.98,158.11],[158.11,158.31],[158.31,158.79],[158.79,158.92],[158.92,159.46],[159.46,159.8],[160.03,160.44],[160.44,160.57],[160.57,161.04],[161.04,161.72],[161.72,161.85],[161.85,162.25],[162.49,162.62],[162.62,163.23],[163.23,163.77],[163.77,164.11],[164.11,164.31],[164.31,164.78]]},{"el":"h4","text":"La llamada al 911 usada como arma hoy","start":166.11,"end":169.25,"words":[[166.11,166.27],[166.27,166.74],[166.74,166.9],[166.9,168.08],[168.08,168.47],[168.47,168.79],[168.79,169.1],[169.1,169.26]]},{"el":"s4","text":"En 2018 y 2020, videos mostraron a personas blancas llamando a la policía contra personas negras que hacían una barbacoa (Oakland), esperaban en un Starbucks (Filadelfia, donde arrestaron a dos hombres), vendían agua (San Francisco) y observaban aves (Central Park).","start":169.95,"end":189.55,"words":[[169.97,170.12],[170.12,171.33],[171.33,171.41],[171.41,172.39],[172.66,173.11],[173.11,173.79],[173.79,173.87],[173.87,174.47],[174.47,175.0],[175.0,175.53],[175.53,175.61],[175.61,175.76],[175.76,176.36],[176.36,176.82],[176.82,177.42],[177.42,177.88],[177.88,178.03],[178.03,178.48],[178.48,178.71],[178.71,179.32],[179.32,179.92],[180.19,180.87],[180.87,181.02],[181.02,181.17],[181.17,181.78],[181.78,182.61],[182.87,183.25],[183.25,183.93],[183.93,184.01],[184.01,184.24],[184.24,184.77],[185.03,185.64],[185.64,185.94],[185.94,186.17],[186.17,186.85],[187.11,187.19],[187.19,187.95],[187.95,188.25],[188.25,188.78],[188.78,189.16]]},{"el":"s4","text":"San Francisco aprobó la Ley CAREN en 2020, después de la ley de Oregón de 2019 y la AB 1775 de California.","start":189.9,"end":199.59,"words":[[189.9,190.11],[190.11,190.75],[190.75,191.18],[191.18,191.32],[191.32,191.53],[191.53,191.89],[191.89,192.03],[192.03,192.95],[193.2,193.7],[193.7,193.84],[193.84,193.98],[193.98,194.2],[194.2,194.34],[194.34,194.76],[194.76,194.91],[194.91,196.04],[196.04,196.11],[196.11,196.26],[196.26,196.4],[196.4,198.32],[198.32,198.46],[198.46,199.24]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Los datos respaldan los videos.","start":199.94,"end":202.46,"words":[[199.99,200.22],[200.22,200.59],[200.59,201.27],[201.27,201.49],[201.49,202.02]]},{"el":"s4","text":"En San Francisco, solo alrededor del 1% de las llamadas por “persona sospechosa” del último año terminó en arresto, multa o informe.","start":202.81,"end":211.61,"words":[[202.83,202.97],[202.97,203.17],[203.17,203.85],[204.09,204.36],[204.36,204.97],[204.97,205.18],[205.18,205.99],[205.99,206.13],[206.13,206.33],[206.33,206.81],[206.81,207.01],[207.01,207.49],[207.49,208.17],[208.17,208.37],[208.37,208.78],[208.78,208.98],[208.98,209.46],[209.46,209.6],[209.6,210.07],[210.31,210.65],[210.65,210.72],[210.72,211.26]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La Encuesta federal de Contacto entre la Policía y el Público (2020) halló que las personas negras que tuvieron contacto con la policía tenían casi tres veces más probabilidades que las blancas de sufrir amenazas o uso de la fuerza.","start":211.96,"end":227.79,"words":[[211.97,212.12],[212.12,212.74],[212.74,213.27],[213.27,213.43],[213.43,214.04],[214.04,214.42],[214.42,214.57],[214.57,215.19],[215.19,215.26],[215.26,215.42],[215.42,215.95],[215.95,216.87],[217.14,217.45],[217.45,217.6],[217.6,217.83],[217.83,218.44],[218.44,218.9],[218.9,219.05],[219.05,219.67],[219.67,220.28],[220.28,220.51],[220.51,220.66],[220.66,221.28],[221.28,221.81],[221.81,222.12],[222.12,222.42],[222.42,222.81],[222.81,223.04],[223.04,224.11],[224.11,224.26],[224.26,224.49],[224.49,225.03],[225.03,225.18],[225.18,225.64],[225.64,226.25],[226.25,226.33],[226.33,226.56],[226.56,226.71],[226.71,226.87],[226.87,227.4]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Lo que funciona","start":228.69,"end":229.88,"words":[[228.69,228.86],[228.86,229.03],[229.03,229.72]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Las ciudades están enviando equipos capacitados en lugar de policías armados a muchas llamadas.","start":230.58,"end":236.98,"words":[[230.61,230.83],[230.83,231.42],[231.42,231.79],[231.79,232.38],[232.38,232.82],[232.82,233.64],[233.64,233.78],[233.78,234.15],[234.15,234.3],[234.3,234.96],[234.96,235.48],[235.48,235.55],[235.55,236.0],[236.0,236.59]]},{"el":"s5","text":"El programa CAHOOTS de Eugene, Oregón, lo hace desde 1989.","start":237.33,"end":243.3,"words":[[237.33,237.47],[237.47,238.04],[238.04,238.46],[238.46,238.61],[238.61,239.1],[239.35,239.85],[240.09,240.24],[240.24,240.45],[240.45,240.8],[240.8,242.79]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Un estudio de 2022 en Science Advances halló que el programa STAR de Denver redujo las denuncias de los delitos menores que atendía.","start":243.65,"end":252.9,"words":[[243.67,243.81],[243.81,244.33],[244.33,244.48],[244.48,245.6],[245.6,245.74],[245.74,246.19],[246.19,246.78],[246.78,247.08],[247.08,247.23],[247.23,247.38],[247.38,247.97],[247.97,248.27],[248.27,248.42],[248.42,248.86],[248.86,249.31],[249.31,249.53],[249.53,250.2],[250.2,250.35],[250.35,250.57],[250.57,251.09],[251.09,251.61],[251.61,251.76],[251.76,252.42]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Una Ley CAREN federal añade la otra mitad: una consecuencia por usar a la policía como arma.","start":253.25,"end":259.39,"words":[[253.3,253.51],[253.51,253.73],[253.73,254.08],[254.08,254.58],[254.58,254.93],[254.93,255.08],[255.08,255.36],[255.36,255.79],[256.03,256.25],[256.25,257.1],[257.1,257.31],[257.31,257.6],[257.6,257.67],[257.67,257.81],[257.81,258.38],[258.38,258.66],[258.66,259.02]]}]}